1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,400
Every day, students walk past broken things on campus — Wi-Fi that drops, heaters that die, railings that wobble. This is UniFix.

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:17,400
Today, reporting a problem means hunting for the right office, filling out a form, and never hearing back. So most problems just never get reported.

3
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:26,700
UniFix fixes that. Students say what's wrong in plain words, and it goes straight to the one team that can fix it.

4
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:33,300
We built it for the Hackachusetts Civic Action challenge V4, better college experiences. Here's the student view.

5
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:38,100
The campus feed shows what's open, what's urgent, and what's already fixed.

6
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:42,200
The live map shows where problems cluster, colored by severity.

7
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:48,700
Click any bubble to see every report inside it.

8
00:00:48,800 --> 00:01:01,400
First, quality. Spam, jokes, and claims like “I won a million dollars” are blocked before they reach staff — so every report in the queue is real.

9
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:05,300
But safety beats everything. Ari reads as you type.

10
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:14,700
The moment something sounds like an emergency, UniFix shows Call 911 and campus police instantly — before any AI runs. It never dials for you.

11
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:18,400
Now a real report. Just say what's wrong.

12
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:21,600
AI picks the team, then asks only what's missing.

13
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:23,900
Wi-Fi is everywhere — so, no specific place.

14
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Ari checks the past: nine similar reports, usually fixed in about three days — and suggests quick fixes first.

15
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:32,400
Add a photo if you like,

16
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:35,700
check the card, and post.

17
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:41,500
It's rated Medium and sent to the IT team — and only IT staff can see it.

18
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:51,300
On the staff side, each team sees only its own area, ranked by severity times how many students are affected — not by who complains loudest.

19
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:57,000
If something's unclear, staff can message the reporter directly.

20
00:01:57,100 --> 00:02:03,700
They can post public updates, then mark it solved. Everyone who co-signed is notified automatically.

21
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:14,300
The student gets a notification. One click opens the conversation, and they answer right there — no emails, no forms, no lost tickets.

22
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:17,800
A misunderstanding becomes a two-minute chat.

23
00:02:17,900 --> 00:02:24,300
We built UniFix with Kiro: specs, steering, hooks, skills and Kiro Crew — backed by over three hundred tests.

24
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:30,300
UniFix works for any Massachusetts campus. Try it yourself — no login needed.
